# Task 7 Report: Provider-Neutral Authorized Role Lifecycle

## Outcome

Task 7 is implemented in the approved V5 source boundary:

- `core/pit_optimizer_v5/provider.py` is the new provider-neutral domain and orchestration module.
- `core/pit_optimizer_authorization.py` has no content change from `HEAD`. The proposed structural
  legacy authorization change was reverted after audit because it would weaken the existing V3/V4
  concrete-owner and registry checks. V5 authorization remains a separate typed lifecycle.

No test, evaluator, runtime, CLI, gateway, Docker, replay, data, or filesystem-repository file was
added or modified. No live provider call was made.

## Closed role authority and binding

- `RoleSchemaAuthorityV5` owns exact immutable canonical schema bytes plus the role-specific
  manifest-derived cardinality, tunable-axis/variant limits, full-source permission, and author
  policy-scope/path authority. Its digest is derived from that complete authority; requests cannot
  substitute a mutable schema mapping or infer limits from prompt text.
- `RoleRequestV5` binds one role, canonical aggregate-only input, issued evidence, complete expected
  parent/hypothesis/experiment/discovery-plan identity, the schema authority, and output limit.
- The manifest constructor derives this authority from validated `CampaignManifestV5` and
  `PolicyScopeV5` values. Investigator, author, and critic inputs each have a closed role-specific
  envelope. Author input is restricted to the exact editable files authorized by policy scope; all
  four source files require manifest-enabled full-source escape.
- Outbound evidence is not an arbitrary nested JSON value. It must be the existing bounded
  `RoleEvidenceV5` numeric/null aggregate projection, while role context must be one exact frozen
  `InvestigatorRoleInputV5`, `AuthorRoleInputV5`, or `CriticRoleInputV5` value. `RoleRequestV5`
  derives its immutable messages, evidence digests, and issued-evidence records from those values;
  callers cannot inject a separately authored message envelope.
- `parse_and_bind_role_artifact` duplicate-rejects JSON keys, validates closed role schemas and exact
  primitive types without coercion, then canonicalizes accepted provider JSON for authenticated
  persistence. Whitespace and key order are not incorrectly treated as semantic failures.
- Investigator ranks/cardinality/evidence citations, author parent/hypothesis/policy scope and
  structural-template caps, and critic complete ordered experiment/evidence batches are checked
  against request authority. Artifact structure/cardinality/cap failures classify as
  `response_schema`; unknown evidence or echoed identity disagreement classifies as
  `evidence_binding`.
- Tagged floats are represented as finite canonical round-tripping hexadecimal strings consistently
  in both schema and parser. Decimal, tuple, enum, and null representations use existing exact V5
  canonical primitives.

## One-shot provider and durable lifecycle

- `CompletionProvider.complete_once` accepts a neutral `ProviderCompletionRequestV5` and returns a
  closed `CompletionResultV5`. Results include the exact returned model, authoritative nonnegative
  Decimal USD cost, exact input/output tokens, provider request identity, response-received state,
  and `external_attempt_count == 1`.
- `OneShotJsonCompletionV5` and `GatewayCompletionProviderV5` form a truthful structural adapter
  boundary. The adapter sends the authenticated schema bytes and explicitly requests zero automatic
  retries and zero schema-repair calls. It does not claim compatibility with a nonexistent method on
  the current V4 gateway.
- `RoleAuthorizationLifecycleV5` defines durable reserve, slot verification, terminal settlement,
  unreported-attempt reconciliation, recovery, and receipt verification. Slot and receipt values
  authenticate the request, authorization, prior and cumulative attempts/tokens/USD, terminal
  sequence, attempt facts, and settlement identity.
- `AuthorizedRoleRunnerV5` reserves one distinct manifest-authorized primary/retry/repair slot,
  verifies it, invokes the provider exactly once, parses through the shared binder, and verifies the
  terminal receipt. Retries and repairs default to zero and can only use separately authorized
  attempt kinds.
- Model substitution, hidden/multiple external attempts, per-call or cumulative token/USD overage,
  malformed or duplicate slot responses, and mismatched receipts fail typed. Any slot returned after
  successful reserve is terminally settled or recovered; transport uncertainty uses the lifecycle's
  reconciliation boundary and cannot silently abandon accounting authority.
- Stable failures contain only closed role/code fields. Provider exception messages and types do not
  enter stable identities. Neutral usage facts are recorded for success, schema/binding failure,
  transport failure, and recovered outcomes.
- `FixtureRoleRunnerV5` consumes deterministic local responses through the same parser/binder and
  emits exact provider-free zero-call/zero-token/zero-cost facts.

