The available focused legacy test selection was also attempted. All selected cases stopped in the
shared pre-target V2 fixture at `core/pit_optimization_contract.py:3698` with
`ValueError: worst role section cannot reach its canonical cap`, before any provider or
authorization assertion ran. This pre-existing stale-fixture failure was not changed outside Task 7
scope. The planned `tests/test_pit_optimizer_v5_runtime.py` does not exist at this revision, and the
user override forbids adding a substitute.

## Deferred production composition

Task 7 intentionally defines, but does not fabricate, a durable ledger implementation. Task 9 must
compose `AuthorizedRoleRunnerV5` with a real ledger-backed `RoleAuthorizationLifecycleV5` and a
truthful production implementation of `OneShotJsonCompletionV5`. That implementation must preserve
reserve/settle/recover authentication and authoritative returned-model/token/USD/attempt facts. The
current V4 gateway and its concrete authorization registry remain unchanged until that focused
composition exists.

## Security review correction

The scoped review found that the original aggregate-only gate still accepted arbitrary nested
mappings and depended on a blacklist. The provider boundary now fails closed structurally:

- investigator archive-family and prior-critic context use frozen tagged aggregate records and only
  reference the exact issued metric evidence;
- author input is a typed hypothesis, typed V3 policy-contract authority, and an exact tuple of
  validated `SourceFileV5` values;
- critic input is an ordered complete batch of tagged evaluation-scenario, prediction, semantic
  comparison, and typed-failure aggregate records;
- all supplied `RoleEvidenceV5` items must use the closed provider metric namespace, every issued ID
  must be referenced by the role-specific input, and no unreferenced payload can be added; and
- explicit prose fields retain a defense-in-depth scanner for symbol-like tokens embedded in text,
  common credential formats, concatenated sensitive names, and Windows/POSIX paths. Exact
  policy-scope-authorized source text is the sole content-scanning exemption.

`task7 closed aggregate security smoke: ok` covered valid investigator/author/critic construction,
deterministic request identity, shared fixture parsing, initial empty archive/critic context,
authorized source transmission, and representative existing aggregate metric IDs. It also rejected
the former arbitrary mapping/payload surface, `{day, value}` rows, `mytickerdata`/`secretvalue`,
unreferenced evidence, non-namespaced metrics, embedded ticker lists, password/token material,
Windows/POSIX paths, and a mismatched critic experiment batch. No provider call or test-file change
was made.

## Ordered citation and parent-source correction

The final scoped re-review identified two remaining request-authority gaps, now closed in
`provider.py`:

- Role citations no longer pass through sets. The controller defines one role-specific ordered
  citation tuple: investigator evaluator evidence followed by archive-family and critic-direction
  rows; author hypothesis citations; and critic evaluation-scenario evidence followed by semantic
  and typed-failure evidence. That flattened tuple must be globally duplicate-free and equal the
  issued `RoleEvidenceV5` tuple exactly, including order. Reuse across aggregate records or role
  sections and reordered/extra/missing evidence now fail request construction.
- `AuthorPolicyContractsV5` now carries the complete exact `PolicyRevisionIdentityV5` instead of
  independently supplied interface/runtime/constraint digests. Every authorized `SourceFileV5`
  path and exact UTF-8 SHA-256 must match the corresponding digest in the parent's canonical
  four-file source map, and the request binding's `parent_revision_sha256` must equal the digest
  derived from that full parent identity. A caller can no longer pair an opaque parent digest with
  unrelated but syntactically valid source bytes.

`task7 ordered citation and parent source binding smoke: ok` covered exact-order positive controls
for all three roles, reordered investigator/author/critic evidence, cross-record investigator reuse,
cross-section critic reuse, an authenticated source subset, exact four-file full-source escape, a
valid one-byte source mutation rejected against the original identity, an unrelated binding digest,
shared fixture parsing, embedded ticker and credential rejection, and the valid source-content
scanner exemption. Fresh compile, Ruff, export, coupling, source-diff, and legacy-authorization
checks passed without a provider call or test-file change.
